# 💬 Online Web Chat Application

A real-time web chat application built with Python and Flask-SocketIO.
Multiple users can connect and chat simultaneously. Includes an admin system to monitor and kick users.

---

## 🚀 Features

- Real-time messaging using WebSocket protocol
- User join/leave notifications
- Online users list
- Admin login system
- Kick & ban users (kicked users cannot rejoin)
- Accessible over the internet via ngrok

---

## 🛠️ Technologies Used

| Technology | Purpose |
|---|---|
| Python | Server-side language |
| Flask | Web framework |
| Flask-SocketIO | WebSocket support |
| HTML/CSS/JavaScript | Frontend (client side) |
| jQuery | DOM manipulation |
| Socket.IO (JS) | Client-side WebSocket |
| ngrok | Public URL tunneling |

---

## 📁 Project Structure


project/
├── denem1.py          # Flask server
└── templates/
    └── index.html     # Frontend (HTML + JS + CSS)


---

## ⚙️ Installation & Setup

**1. Clone the repository:**

git clone https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/online-web-chat.git
cd online-web-chat

**2. Create a virtual environment:**

python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate


**3. Install dependencies:**
bash
pip install flask flask-socketio


**4. Run the server:**

python denem1.py


**5. Open in browser:**

http://localhost:5000


---

## 🌐 Public Access (ngrok)

To make the chat accessible from outside your network:


ngrok http 5000


Share the generated URL with others to connect from anywhere.

---

## 👮 Admin System

- Open the chat and log in with a username
- In the sidebar, enter the admin password: `admin123`
- Click **Login** to activate admin mode
- **Kick** buttons will appear next to each user
- Kicked users are banned and cannot rejoin with the same username

---

## 🔧 How It Works

1. The Flask server runs on port 5000
2. Clients connect via WebSocket using Socket.IO
3. When a message is sent, the server broadcasts it to all connected clients
4. Each user has a unique Session ID (SID)
5. Admin can disconnect any user by targeting their SID
6. Banned users are stored in a list and blocked on reconnect attempt

---

## ⚠️ Limitations

- Messages are stored in memory and lost when the server restarts
- No database integration (future improvement: SQLite)
- Admin password is hardcoded (future improvement: proper authentication)

